Polybot - Third-party attributions
==================================

This project incorporates curated data or design patterns from the following
third-party works. Code in this repository is original unless otherwise noted;
these attributions are retained for provenance.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. koala73/worldmonitor
   https://github.com/koala73/worldmonitor
   (c) 2024-2026 Elie Habib
   Licensed under GNU AGPL-3.0

   USED FOR:
       - Curated RSS/Atom feed URL list in lib/news_feeds.py
       - Source-tiering concept (market-moving wire services ranked first)

   WHAT WE DID NOT COPY:
       - No worldmonitor source code, parsing logic, UI, or proxy helpers
       - Feed URLs are factual data (URLs to public third-party feeds) and
         are not themselves copyrightable

   AGPL-3.0 caveat: because AGPL SS13 imposes network-copyleft on any code
   linked or served over a network, worldmonitor's *code* cannot be imported
   into this project without open-sourcing the entire bot. We chose to
   re-implement any feed-handling logic from scratch rather than vendor
   their code. Before any COMMERCIAL or HOSTED deployment of polybot,
   review whether the curated feed list should be replaced with
   independently sourced URLs, or worldmonitor should be commercially
   licensed.

